SKILL_DOC = """---
name: breadboard-ops
description: >
  Operate the Breadboard K3s cluster, emulators, and Fullsend agent execution stack on rhea.
  Use when inspecting cluster status, querying emulator tickets, monitoring Actions workflow
  runs and logs, resetting OpenShell state, or running conformance seeders.
---

# Breadboard Operations Guide

Authoritative, version-matched operational guide for Breadboard on physical host `rhea`.

## 1. CLI Subcommands (`scripts/bb`)

`scripts/bb` is the deterministic AXI/TOON-compliant operations tool.

- `./scripts/bb`: Content-first home view showing cluster pod health, node temperature, emulator ticket totals, runner statuses, and recent workflow runs.
- `./scripts/bb --skill`: Emits this complete version-matched operational guide.
- `./scripts/bb status`: Detailed TOON status of physical node thermal readings, K3s workload pods across namespaces, OpenShell profiles, OpenShell providers, sandboxes, and tickets.
- `./scripts/bb runs [--repo <owner/repo>|all] [--limit <n>]`: List Actions workflow runs for a repository (default: `fullsend-dev/triage-target`, or `--repo all` across triage and cve targets).
- `./scripts/bb logs <run_id> [--repo <owner/repo>] [--job <name>] [--full]`: Pre-computes the job summary table, automatically selects the first failed job (or `Triage` / `--job <name>` if none failed), and displays its log. Truncates to last 1500 characters by default unless `--full` is specified.
- `./scripts/bb tickets [--source github|gitlab|jira] [--limit <n>]`: Queries `https://dashboard.<domain>/api/tickets` and returns ticket counts and TOON rows.
- `./scripts/bb openshell [status|reset]`: `status` displays gateway pod, profiles, providers, and sandboxes. `reset` scales `sts/openshell` to 0, deletes PVC `openshell-data-openshell-0`, and scales back to 1.
- `./scripts/bb seed <demo|cve|conformance>`: Deterministically runs ticket seeder (`scripts/seed_demo_tickets.py`), CVE fixture seeder (`deploy/fullsend/seed/seed-cve-fixture.py`), or end-to-end conformance triage (`deploy/scripts/24-run-conformance-triage.sh --keep-issue`).

## 2. The 3 Fullsend Patch Layers

Breadboard maintains three distinct, non-overlapping patch layers to bridge upstream Fullsend with the local emulator and OpenShell environment:

1. **Go Build-Time Layer (`deploy/scripts/05i-build-fullsend.sh` & embedded profile `0016`)**:
   - Patches Go source code in `checkouts/fullsend-ai/fullsend` before compiling the `fullsend` binary.
   - Includes private forge resolution (`0005`, `0006`, `0007`), token scoping on private enterprise forges (`0008`), harness environment propagation (`0009`), custom runner name addressing (`0011`, `0012`, `0013`, `0014`, `0015`), and embedded GitHub read-only profile `0016` to allow emulator endpoints without external network egress.
   - Publishes the compiled binary to `deploy/fullsend/vendor/fullsend` for release asset seeding.

2. **Workflow Mirror Layer (`deploy/fullsend/seed/seed-upstream-fullsend.py`)**:
   - Mirrors the reusable Actions workflows, composite actions, and scripts from `fullsend-ai/fullsend` into the emulator repository.
   - Applies `MIRROR_PATCHES` (such as `0003-honor-github-api-and-server-url.patch` and `0004-skip-local-sandbox-host-setup.patch`) to files read by workflow dispatch at run time. Patches here never touch Go source.

3. **Agent Harness Mirror Layer (`deploy/fullsend/seed/seed-upstream-agents.py`)**:
   - Mirrors the full `fullsend-ai/agents` repository into the emulator.
   - Applies harness `MIRROR_PATCHES` (`0001` through `0005` under `deploy/fullsend/patches/agents/`), which configure GitHub host addresses, pass forge tokens into sandboxes, and select CA-bearing sandbox images. Patches here affect only what agent harnesses read at runtime.

## 3. Physical Host `rhea` Hardware & Thermal Rules

`rhea` is an amd64 Fedora 44 physical host operating with fanless, passive cooling.

- **Thermal Boundary**: CPU core temperatures must remain strictly below 90°C. Normal idle temperature is 35°C–45°C.
- **Strictly Sequential Builds**: Heavy compilation tasks (OpenShell Rust compiler, Go binary builds, container image generation) must run strictly sequentially. Never run parallel builds.
- **Enforced Build Flags**:
  - `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2`: Caps rustc parallel jobs to prevent thermal throttling.
  - `PODMAN_SUDO=1`: Uses root podman to avoid rootless storage driver bottlenecks and CPU spin.
  - `SKIP_SANDBOX_DEV=1`: Skips redundant sandbox development images when only host/local images are needed.

## 4. OpenShell 0.1.4 Architecture

OpenShell 0.1.4 operates in `openshell-system` and orchestrates sandboxes in `ai-pipeline`:

- **Distroless Gateway & Supervisor**:
  - The gateway runs in `openshell-0` StatefulSet.
  - The supervisor runs in its own container alongside each sandbox and verifies upstream TLS against its own image's certificate bundle.
- **`openshell-supervisor-local:k3s` CA Trust**:
  - Because OpenShell 0.1.4 supervisor containers cannot dynamically mount external CA certificates without proxy configuration, `deploy/scripts/05i-build-fullsend.sh` builds `openshell-supervisor-local:k3s` from `ghcr.io/nvidia/openshell/supervisor` with the internal CA certificate (`/tmp/rhea-ca.crt`) appended directly into the image's trust store.
- **`gcp-credentials` Dummy Placeholder Rule**:
  - Workloads and provider profiles requiring Google Cloud / Vertex AI inference declare volume mounts for Kubernetes secret `gcp-credentials`.
  - When real Google ADC credentials are not configured, a dummy placeholder secret containing standard service-account JSON structure must be maintained so pods mount the volume and schedule successfully without container crashes.
"""

